    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>99 Myrtle Avenue<lb/>
                        <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__1444" type="place">Hamilton</rs>, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__1043" type="place">Ont.</rs>
                        <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__849" type="place">CANADA</rs><lb/><date
                            when="1947-03-05">March 5th, 1947</date>.</dateline><salute>Dear <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I have been invited to give a lecture on Existentialism at the Philosophical Club
                    of the College of the City of <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New
                        York</rs> on <date when="1947-03-27">March 27th</date>. For the preparation
                    of this lecture, I should very much like to consult your views as expressed in
                    the Journal of the History of Ideas about a year ago.<note type="ea">Gemeint
                        ist: <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>: <rs
                            ref="#tillich__IGG2446U" type="work">Existential Philosophy</rs>
                        (1944).</note> However, I find this Journal unavailable here, and not
                    available at the University of <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__1082" type="place"
                        >Toronto</rs> for another month or two. I wonder, therefore whether you
                    could be so very kind as to loan me an offprint of that article. I could return
                    it to you as soon as I have completed my lecture. If you do have an offprint at
                    hand and can send it to me, I should appreciate it if you could let me have it
                    soon, as I do not have much time left.</p>
                <p>I should like to say again that I was very happy to make your acquaintance during
                    my recent visit in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs>,
                    and I do hope to be able to have a talk with you soon again. I was, of course,
                    especially glad to hear from you the good news about your nephew <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__1922" type="person"
                    >Ernst</rs>.<!-- <note type="ea">Es ist nicht klar, worauf sich <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4926" type="person">Fackenheim</rs> hier bezieht.</note> --></p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Hoping that I am not giving you too much trouble,<lb/>I am,<lb/>Yours
                        sincerely,</salute>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rend="hand"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4926" type="person">Emil L.
                                Fackenheim</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4926"
                            type="person">Emil L. Fackenheim</rs>.</signed>
                </closer>

            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
